course: dictionary
lesson: 15904
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Unmatched» is one of them. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the author wants.
explain: «Her skill on the piano was unmatched in the whole school.» Here there is nobody as good as her, so unmatched means better than all others. «I found three socks in the drawer, but they were all unmatched.» Here there is no pair for any sock, so unmatched means not paired.
explain: Always ask: what does the rest of the sentence say? Then try each meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Unmatched» means better than all others, with no equal: «unmatched skill».
fact: «Unmatched» also means not paired or not matching: «unmatched socks».
fact: In maths, some items are left unmatched after pairing, so counting them shows the difference between two groups.
fact: «Unmatched» is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a person, a sock or a skill.
exercise: «Her skill on the piano was unmatched in the whole school.» What does unmatched mean here? | Not paired with a partner | Played too loudly | Played in a different key | * Better than all the others
exercise: «I found three socks in the drawer, but they were all unmatched.» What does unmatched mean here? | * Not paired, with no matching sock | Lost forever in the wash | Very clean and new | Better than all the others
exercise: «The unmatched socks sat in a pile by the washing machine.» Find and copy one word that tells you the socks have no pair. | pair | * unmatched | washing | socks
test: In maths the class sorted the cards, and six were unmatched. What does unmatched mean here? | The best cards in the class | * Left over with no pair | Counted twice by mistake | Shuffled into a pile
test: A shop advert says «Unmatched comfort for your feet». What does unmatched praise? | Made of soft wool | Very cheap for the money | Not paired, so only one shoe | * Better than any other, with no equal
exam: Which sentence uses unmatched to mean the best, with no equal? | The socks in the drawer are unmatched | The two mittens were unmatched in the bag | The painting lay on the floor, unmatched | * The goalkeeper's reflexes are unmatched
